+# Cancellation
+
+For whoever changes when a member may cancel a pantry order, or answers a member whose cancellation was refused. A
+member may cancel a pantry order until 2 hours before its pickup slot starts; after that the app refuses, and the
+member calls the pantry instead. The cutoff shipped in October 2026, after late cancellations left packed bags on
+the shelf three Saturdays in a row and 25 bags of fresh food were thrown away in a week.
+
+## The cutoff
+
+`can_cancel` in `larder/cancellation.py` allows a cancellation while the current time is earlier than 2 hours before
+the pickup slot starts, `CUTOFF` in the same file. From exactly 2 hours before the slot onward it refuses.
+
+For a pickup slot starting at 17:00:
+
+| Member cancels at | Result  |
+|-------------------|---------|
+| 14:59             | allowed |
+| 15:00             | refused |
+| 16:50             | refused |
+
+## Why 2 hours
+
+Volunteers start packing a slot's bags 2 hours before it starts. A cancellation before that costs the pantry nothing;
+one after it leaves a packed bag on the shelf. In early October 2026 members were cancelling minutes before their
+slot, such as at 16:50 for a 17:00 pickup, after their bags were packed. One Saturday was the third in a row
+with bags left over, 9 that day, all with milk, bread and greens; by October 7, 25 bags of fresh food had been thrown
+away that month. An in-app banner asking members to cancel earlier had run since the summer without changing that.
+The cutoff therefore matches the start of the packing shift, and a member who cannot come after it calls the pantry,
+where the volunteers decide.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- **No refusal message in the repository.** `can_cancel` only answers yes or no. The pantry agreed to the cutoff on
+  the condition that the refusal shows the pantry's phone number, and neither that message nor the number is in this
+  repository. Until it is, check where the refusal is shown before telling a member they will see the number there.
